msgctxt "power.diplomacy.aid.send.label"
msgid "Send state aid"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.diplomacy.aid.send.means"
msgid "Give money or goods to another country's Treasury, on the public record, for a stated purpose."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.diplomacy.message.send.label"
msgid "Send official messages"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.diplomacy.message.send.means"
msgid "Send messages to other governments in this country's name. Diplomatic mail is private between the two states."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.diplomacy.treaty.break.label"
msgid "Break treaties"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.diplomacy.treaty.break.means"
msgid "Walk out of an agreement this country signed. It is recorded permanently, and everyone can see who broke what."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.diplomacy.treaty.propose.label"
msgid "Propose treaties"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.diplomacy.treaty.propose.means"
msgid "Offer another country a formal agreement, whether alliance, trade or peace, that binds this one if they accept it."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.diplomacy.treaty.ratify.label"
msgid "Accept treaties"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.diplomacy.treaty.ratify.means"
msgid "Accept a treaty another country has offered, which makes its terms binding on this one."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.government.bank.create.label"
msgid "Found a national bank"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.government.bank.create.means"
msgid "Licence a bank to take deposits and lend inside this country."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.government.budget.manage.label"
msgid "Set budgets"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.government.budget.manage.means"
msgid "Draw up what the state intends to spend and on what. A budget is a public plan, not a payment: the money still moves under a separate authority."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.government.citizenship.decide.label"
msgid "Admit citizens"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.government.citizenship.decide.means"
msgid "Approve or refuse applications to become a citizen here. Only matters where the country has chosen approval over automatic admission."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.government.discord.manage.label"
msgid "Link Discord"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.government.discord.manage.means"
msgid "Connect this country to a Discord server for announcements."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.government.election.manage.label"
msgid "Call a referendum"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.government.election.manage.means"
msgid "Ask the whole country a question with two to six answers. The result changes no law by itself. Elections need nobody to call them: every seat goes to its electorate on its own schedule."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.government.infrastructure.manage.label"
msgid "Open public works"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.government.infrastructure.manage.means"
msgid "Commission transport, industrial or civil works in a province, paid for from the Treasury and the national stockpile. It is what makes a province produce more."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.government.law.enact.label"
msgid "Enact laws"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.government.law.enact.means"
msgid "Sign what the chamber has carried. The world does this on its own within the minute, so it is rarely used by hand."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.government.law.propose.label"
msgid "Propose bills"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.government.law.propose.means"
msgid "Put a bill before the chamber for it to vote on."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.government.law.vote.label"
msgid "Vote on bills"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.government.law.vote.means"
msgid "Cast one of the chamber's votes. A law vote is public and permanent, unlike an election ballot, which is secret."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.government.office.appoint.label"
msgid "Appoint to offices"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.government.office.appoint.means"
msgid "Put somebody into an office, and form ministries that carry part of your own authority. You cannot grant a power you do not hold."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.government.public_economy.manage.label"
msgid "Run public programmes"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.government.public_economy.manage.means"
msgid "Open and administer subsidies and procurement that citizens and companies apply to, and approve or refuse what they ask for."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.government.research.manage.label"
msgid "Fund research"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.government.research.manage.means"
msgid "Start a tier of national research, which cheapens everything that branch touches for every company in the country, and is the only way to build past level five."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.government.territory.cede.label"
msgid "Give a province back"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.government.territory.cede.means"
msgid "Hand one of this country's provinces to another country, for good. Nothing but the receiving country's own consent can undo it, which makes it the least reversible thing anybody here can do."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.government.treasury.spend.label"
msgid "Spend from the Treasury"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.government.treasury.spend.means"
msgid "Move public money out of the Treasury, to a citizen, a company or another country. Every movement is on the public ledger with the name of whoever authorised it."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.government.world_project.contribute.label"
msgid "Give to world projects"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.government.world_project.contribute.means"
msgid "Commit this country's money and materials to something the whole world is building. The largest contributors are named when it finishes."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.military.asset.commission.label"
msgid "Build heavy assets"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.military.asset.commission.means"
msgid "Order the machines a country fights with, such as aircraft, vehicles and heavy weapons, out of the country's own stores and treasury."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.military.asset.deploy.label"
msgid "Move heavy assets"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.military.asset.deploy.means"
msgid "Send this country's machines to a province, where they take part in whatever is fought there. They can be lost."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.military.battle.launch.label"
msgid "Open battles"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.military.battle.launch.means"
msgid "Start a fight over one province inside a war that is already running. Citizens choose whether to turn up."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.military.order.issue.label"
msgid "Issue orders"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.military.order.issue.means"
msgid "Post a military order with a reward, directing this country's fighters at a battle that matters."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.military.war.declare.label"
msgid "Declare war"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.military.war.declare.means"
msgid "Open a war against another country, which lets this country's citizens fight for territory it claims."
msgstr ""

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
msgctxt "power.military.war.join.label"
msgid "Answer an ally's call"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "power.military.war.join.means"
msgid "Bring this country into a war an ally is already fighting, on the defending side, where a mutual-defence treaty gives the right. It costs nothing to enter and cannot be taken back: from that moment this country's citizens can fight there, and every other country in that war is at war with this one. Refusing is recorded publicly too."
msgstr ""

#. Shown for a power of an office that has no explanation written yet.
